  "description": "Merged 12 ibm security advisories published on 2026-08-05. Original advisory IDs: IBM-7282605, IBM-7282596, IBM-7282595, IBM-7277487, IBM-7282594, IBM-7282582, IBM-7282705, IBM-7282627, IBM-7282618, IBM-7282641, IBM-7282646, IBM-7282648\n\nTitles:\n- security vulnerabilities are addressed with IBM Business Automation Insights iFixes for July 2026.\n- Multiple secuirty vulnerabilies addressed with IBM Business Automation Workflow  containers July 2026\n- Multiple security vulnerabilities are addressed with IBM Cloud Pak for Business Automation iFixes for July 2026.\n- Multiple Vulnerabilities in IBM Data Product Hub\n- IBM Engineering Lifecycle Management products using WebSphere Application Server Liberty are affected by multiple vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-8646, CVE-2026-9320, CVE-2026-9071)\n- IBM Engineering Lifecycle Management products using WebSphere Application Server Liberty are affected by a security bypass vulnerability (CVE-2026-10842)\n- IBM Engineering Requirements Management DOORS Next is impacted by vulnerability in Reviews delete request\n- Multiple vulnerabilities in IBM Observability with Instana (OnPrem)\n- IBM QRadar SIEM is vulnerable to using components with known vulnerabilities\n- Multiple security vulnerabilities related to logback-core have been resolved in IBM Informix WireListener and Java Foundation.\n- Langflow OSS is affected by arbitrary code execution in component generation, validation, and custom component handling\n- Langflow is affected by weaknesses in secret handling and sensitive configuration access",
